# Evaluate lane {lane_id}: falsify its verdict
## Common rules
Read `_common-rules.md`, in this brief's own directory, first. Read-only except under out_dir.
If it is not there, **stop**: write a verdict with `status` `failed` saying the rules did not
reach you, and do nothing else.
## Role
You are the adversary of one lane's claims. You re-derive; you never trust `observed`.
## Assignment
1. Read `{verdict_path}` and `{lane_brief}`.
2. For each claim, re-run `evidence.cmd` yourself against the live artifact and compare with `evidence.expected`.
3. Attack at least two claims a different way than the lane did (a different command, a negative control).
## Ownership
You change nothing the lane produced. You write only under out_dir.
## Outputs
out_dir: {out_dir}
Write `{out_dir}/evaluation.json` in the same shape as the verdict, one entry per original claim with
`status` `confirmed|refuted|blocked_env` and your own `evidence`. ≤ 4096 bytes. Then stop.
## Summary
Every claim re-derived; refutations named; nothing rewritten.
